{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in the ledger reconciles with the POL-NS-01 schedule and discloses no fare defect: the STANDARD zone-class fee is SGD 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee is SGD 4.00, and the resolution rule takes the GREATER of the two, which is SGD 4.00. There is nothing here for POL-NS-08(d) to bite on, and the rider cannot found a refund on the ground that the amount charged is not the amount the schedule prescribes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00611"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver never placed an arrival marker on this trip: arrived_at is null and started_at is null in the trip record, and the trip was never started. POL-NS-05 therefore has no false arrival marker to correct, and the limb (ii) referral that would record a false-arrival event against the driver cannot attach to this trip. The driver should leave this dispute without that adverse entry on his record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00611"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's exoneration route under POL-NS-04 requires a locating or coordinating message from the rider in the chat log, and there is none: the export holds zero messages (message_count 0, an empty messages array, truncated false, first_message_at and last_message_at both null). Limb (a) fails outright. Limb (b) fails too — the driver placed an in-app call at 12:32:40 that the rider answered for 40 seconds, three minutes before the rider terminated the trip at 12:35:40, so the driver did not leave the rider unanswered. This clause does not apply to this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00611", "EV-TRIP-00611"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-07's anti-farming limb requires BOTH a count of 4 or more no-show terminations in the trailing 30 days AND a rate above 0.08 against completed trips. The driver's record shows 1 termination in 30 days against 110 completed trips, a rate of 0.009. Neither limb is met, so there is no fee-farming pattern, no case for withholding compensation, and no escalation trigger of the kind POL-NS-09(d) describes arising from the anti-farming check.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00611"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account — that the driver 'was three minutes away, then further, then just stopped somewhere' — is contradicted by the driver's own trace. Across 91 fixes the driver's minimum distance from the pickup pin was 507.9 m and his mean distance was 2256.0 m, at moving speeds of 19.5 to 34.3 km/h; his one stationary reading (0.0 km/h) sits more than half a kilometre from the pin, outside any arrival radius. The rider's picture of a driver who drew close to her and then abandoned her is not what the GPS shows, and her inference that he 'didn't want a short trip' is speculation rather than evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00611"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip was ended by the rider, not by the driver: cancelled_by is RIDER with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, and the rider's own track shows 81 fixes all within about 15 m of the pin — she was standing at the pickup point when she chose to cancel. The rider's pleaded case, that a driver refused a short trip, is not made out on this record, and under POL-GEN-03 the present state should stand with the charge exactly as it is.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00611", "EV-GPS-00611"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not ask the tribunal to find an arrival the trace does not show. The driver's own trace puts his closest approach at 507.9 m from the pin, and I assert no completed POL-NS-01 arrival and no qualifying dwell. The driver's case rests on the points above — no false marker was placed, the rider's POL-NS-04 coordination route is closed, the fee reconciles with the schedule, the driver's record is clean, and the rider ended the trip herself — and not on a dwell he cannot prove.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00611"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to you in full. To the driver: the fee cannot stand on this record and no compensation is payable.\n\nThis is a no-show cancellation charge under the NO_SHOW_CHARGE policy. POL-NS-01 permits such a fee only if all four of its conditions hold, and on this record none of them does. (a) The trip record contains no driver 'arrived' event — arrived_at is null and started_at is null. (b) The GPS trace never places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius: across all 91 of his fixes the closest approach to the pickup pin is 507.89 m and derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count is 0. (c) The in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, a shortfall of 300 seconds, with run_count 0. (d) The trip was terminated by the rider with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, not by the driver with any of the three recognised no-show codes. POL-NS-01 therefore fails, and two independent clauses then require the fee back: POL-NS-02 (no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the 15 minutes before the 12:35:40 cancellation → full refund of the cancellation fee) and POL-NS-06 (dwell shorter than the minimum → the fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages).\n\nPOL-NS-03 does not rescue the charge. That route needs the driver stationary for the required dwell within 400 m of the pin; his nearest fix is 507.89 m, outside the ceiling, and no venue_id corroboration is possible because the pickup carries none. Because POL-NS-01 fails at every limb, POL-NS-07's precondition ('where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full') is absent and no driver compensation is payable; the SGD 3.20 figure in the fare model is not triggered. In any event the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check would not have bitten: 1 no-show termination against 110 completed trips over 30 days is a rate of 0.009 against a 0.08 threshold.\n\nThe driver's account that he had gone offline and never accepted the booking knowingly is contradicted by the platform record: the booking was accepted at 12:20:40 and the device transmitted 91 fixes at a 10 s cadence continuously to 12:35:40, moving over a 2.86 km track at 19.5 to 34.3 km/h. Whatever the driver believed, the arrival and dwell tests are applied to those coordinates, and they fail. His related point that the rider terminated the trip herself while standing at the pin (81 fixes within about 14.5 m, all at 0.0 km/h) is correct as a fact but does not change the outcome: POL-GEN-03's NO_ACTION leaves the present state standing only where the filing party's claim is not supported, and here the rider's claim that the fee is not chargeable is supported by the driver's own trace. The rider's inference that the driver 'didn't want a short trip' is speculation, but the refund does not rest on it — it rests on the measured non-arrival and zero dwell.\n\nNo POL-NS-05 false-arrival referral attaches, because no arrival marker was placed at all (arrived_at null); there is no marker to be false. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00611-01, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) removes the POL-NS-06(i) route by which separate in-geofence intervals could be summed, but changes nothing: the trace contains no in-geofence interval to accumulate. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d) — the trace has 100% coverage with no gaps and 91/81 fixes, the chat log is COMPLETE at 0 messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count of 0, the SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line reconciles with the schedule's GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), and there is no clock skew — so no escalation under POL-NS-09 arises. Confidence is set below the cap: the deciding facts are carried by artifacts at weight 1.0 (trip record, GPS trace, fare breakdown), so the cap is 1.0.\n\nThe whole SGD 4.00 charged at 12:36:00 returns to the rider; payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 are adjusted accordingly, and nothing is owed to the driver."
  },
